# Homepage marketing

## Picture first
- Each section is led by imagery or visual composition. Short student-facing copy supports the pictures — do not lead with labels, stat strips, or dense paragraphs.
- One job per section: one headline, one short support line, then visuals.

## Hero budget
- Brand `ORI6IN` is the dominant signal.
- Allow only: brand, one headline, one short sentence, one CTA group, full-bleed photo backdrop.
- No floating badges, chips, stickers, or motif icons on the hero.

## Motifs and motion
- Floating SVG motifs (pencil, book, laptop, badge) only outside the hero.
- Prefer CSS keyframes + IntersectionObserver; no framer-motion/lenis for homepage.
- Always respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (disable floats / Ken Burns / stagger).

## Assets
- Reuse `BANNERS`, `programImage`, `avatarFor` from `apps/web/src/lib/media.ts`.
- Prefer local `/public/home` and `/public/programs` images over remote CDNs.
- No GIF files; use CSS/SVG motion instead.

## Tone
- Write for students: concrete verbs, low jargon, no marketing fluff.
